Applied Mitigation Protocols
Asymmetric 3-6-9 Tie-Rod Matrix (18 Rods): 3 rods on Layer 1 (25-min service swap), 6 on Layer 2 (reduces thermal bridging by 33%), and 9 on Layer 3 ($40^\circ$ pitch prevents PEEK creep).


Oil-Less DLC Bore + Carbon-Graphite Rings: Eliminates traditional oil sumps, oil pumps, and viscous drag, maintaining a low friction coefficient ($\mu \le 0.05$).


Indium/Graphite TIM Buffer: Sandwiched between Layers 1 & 2 to absorb up to $200^\circ\text{C}$ of radial differential thermal expansion without crushing the $Bi_2Te_3$ TEG film.


PTFE/Bronze Channel Bushings: Lines all 18 tie-rod pass-through channels to eliminate metal-on-polymer fretting wear under combustion micro-flexing.


Segmented 6-Arc TEG Modules: Divides the $360^\circ$ TEG array into 6 electrically isolated $60^\circ$ modules to prevent circulating eddy currents caused by intake/exhaust temperature deltas.


Forged Bedplate Girdle: A single-piece aluminum/steel composite lower girdle anchors all 18 tie-rods and main bearing caps, isolating the PEEK-CF block from torsional crankshaft twisting.


